Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||11-05-2001||07:48 PM||||I wonder what ..if anything those other springs you put in did for your launch George.<BR>Also Wondering what coilovers in the rear would do as you mentioned you wanted to switch..<P>Hmmmm Points to ponder..<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000008||banditbalz||11-05-2001||08:02 PM||||JM,  The Eibach(?) springs I got from you are more stiff than stock. The car has less of a tendancy to squat at launch. I would tend to think that a car that "squats" transfers more weight to the rear and therefore hooks up better. I don't know jack about physics, but I think softer in the rear is better...<P>Therefore, I need an adjustable suspension such as coil-overs. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Slammed Fiero||11-05-2001||08:55 PM||||Coilovers will just adjust the height not the stifness. You will be able  to raise the rear , thus moving the center of gravity forward. No idea on how to setup a suspension for drag racing. But if you got a better launch this time out the stiffer springs may have helped weight transfer.<P>You need Konis' to adjust the stiffness of the rear setup.<P>I think that if you are experiencing wheelspin as you mentioned you need slicks. I will keep an eye out for some used R1 Autocross slicks. There street legal , you just need a pair of rims to mount them<P>Autocross tires heat up really quickly and would be a lot harder to spin. With my Pirelli Competition tires I can dump the clutch and it doesn't spin the tires even at around 2500rpm<P>The best part. Usually you can get a set about 1/2 worn for around $50  One tire in the trunk , the other where the spare used to be..Off you go tothe strip.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Posthumane||11-05-2001||09:57 PM||||Banditbalz - the stiffer springs are actually better for your launch. The car doesn't squat as much because of the stiffer springs, but the same force is being applied downward on the rears due to the weight transfer. However, since the springs are stiffer and therefore give you less travel per equal force, the weight transfer happens quicker, giving you traction faster. Result - potential for a better launch.||||reg||1
